editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-007/EVENT-LIST.md:52:5. **Day 105, the silence read.** The lodge book's road column with Seln on the Seventh-day (the circuit of M3): the coats on the bell, older men; the post without a knock; nobody at the gate since the cut. Seln: they've stood down because the corridor is on schedule. Log quotes the packet line: *why spend a team when the seat will deliver him at the year's close.* Seln writes his weekly return at the copying table — true and empty (*Subject remained in residence for the house's recess…*) — and files the duplicate.
