    61	---
    62	
    63	**Finding two — the strata, kept honest.**
    64	
    65	She dated the cache's oldest documents against her own research, and she did it physically, in front of them, because a dating is only as good as the room's ability to check it.
    66	
    67	Paper stock, first: the oldest memorandum's laid sheet against the founding-era compilation's, held up together to the lamp, the same chain-line spacing and the same faint watermark neither of them could identify. Type-face, second: three sorts in the memorandum with the same broken foot as three sorts in the standardization directive's transcribed source, which meant one press, or two presses supplied from one foundry, within a working generation. Seal format, third: the pre-reform registry seal with the outer ring, discontinued in a year Karis named without checking. Vocabulary, fourth, and the one she trusted most, because vocabulary was where an institution's hand showed: a cluster of eleven administrative constructions shared between the memorandum and the directive that appeared nowhere in the registry's language forty years later.
    68	
    69	Then she set down the third document, and touched it once before she let it go.
    70	
    71	"Same era. Same administrative hand." She had all three fanned under the lamp: the oldest memorandum's *corrective classification at Kindling*, the standardization directive's own founding text, and the copied Greyvane passage. "The falsification modification, the standardization directive that discouraged the assay clause into disuse, and the retirement of the old word — [UNBOUND] — are the same era, the same authors. The scheme's founders retired the word when they buried what it described. They didn't need it anymore. Once the corrections function was rewriting the architecture at Kindling, there were no more of them left to name, because the machinery unmade them at the door. The word became a description of a thing that no longer occurred, so they let it fall out of the vocabulary, and wrote the directive that made the whole older stratum unfashionable, so that no one would go looking in it."
    72	
    73	She did not say the word again, that night or afterward.
    74	
    75	"Three acts," she said. "Close the door. Remove the exit. Delete the name of what used to come through. That's not three policies. That's one policy with three instruments, drafted by people sitting in the same room, and I can show you the room's paper."
    76	
    77	And then the boundary, stated as method, because keeping mysteries distinct was what she was for.
    78	
    79	"Here is the limit, and I am entering it as a limit and not a finding, because the difference is the whole of my discipline." She squared her hands on the table. "The falsification is two hundred years old. The cache proves it — the modification, its direction, its function, its contingency. But the sub-layer the modification is *written into* is older. Demonstrably older: the maintenance leaf maintains a layer it did not build. Read its own grammar. It is a service instruction. It says *the function shall be appended to* — appended, to a thing already there. It refers to the layer the way a millwright refers to a river. Nowhere in it does anyone claim to have made anything. The cache documents the modification. It does not document the layer."
    80	
    81	"Then who did make it?" Lira asked.
    82	
    83	"That is exactly the question, and my answer is that I do not know, and that I can prove I cannot know from these documents." Karis's voice did not change at all, which was how they knew she meant it as method and not as caution. "Who built the sub-layer, and when, and why the old word's danger was a danger at all — none of that is in these files, and nothing in an operative's two-century paper trail can reach it, because Seln's files are operational, and the layer beneath the operation is not a thing operations touch. If I put a guess in the register tonight, the guess gets read as a finding by whoever opens the register in ten years, and then we have done to ourselves in miniature exactly what was done to that girl in the river town: written a plausible thing over a true unknown and let the record carry it forward."
    84	
    85	She squared the three documents.
