   157	The other thing arrived that night, in writing, long before it would arrive in the body — and Cael wrote it slowly, in the new satchel, because it was the sentence the whole term had been walking toward and it deserved the pen's full attention:
   158	
   159	*I spent three years proving I could work within the system. Tonight I read the system's maintenance records. It isn't broken. It's maintained. The system was never designed to include me — it was designed, by name, before my name, to correct me at the door, and I'm only here at all because I'm the case the corrector couldn't parse. Every session I've won inside the instrument, I won by accident, in the one stratum the machinery can't reach, and the whole proceedings exist to walk me out of it.*
   160	
