   166	
   167	Lira was on the stair when he came out with the satchel over his shoulder, sitting three steps up with her strapped foot straight out in front of her, giving no indication whatever that she was waiting.
   168	
   169	She had been turning the case over since the third bell and had got it down to one sentence, and she gave him the sentence instead of a greeting, because it was the only part of the night that was any use to anybody.
   170	
   171	"Stop calling it a case." She came up onto the good foot. "It's not evidence. It's a map."

