    30	
    31	The landing beat was late. It was not late by much, only by the length of a step, but the whole of Lira's fighting was built on that beat, the instant after a burst when the floor took her weight and gave it back and she could go again. She had it on the left foot, half a pace past where she had meant to be, facing a little the wrong way. The place where the hip was going to be was behind her.
    32	
    33	The Current girl came round the rest of her bend and found nobody in her way. She looked surprised, and put out her hand as she went by, almost apologetically, and touched Lira on the back of the shoulder.
    34	
