    42	
    43	She did not run the count the second time.
    44	
    45	The flags dropped, and she stood for one beat with her weight on both feet, and on the second she simply went. There was no lie in it at all. Burst two, flat and hard, straight across the Current girl's glide at the hip, the plain rude line that every drill in the red book told a Wind never to take against a Current, because you would arrive before she had bent and she would bend round you.
    46	
    47	The Current girl had been waiting for the lie. She had her weight laid ready to be pulled, and she was pulled by nothing, and for half a beat she was a tall girl standing on a floor instead of a thing moving over one. Lira came down in front of her on the left foot, which was where that line happened to end, and the landing beat was clean, and her palm was on the Current girl's hip before the bend began.
