     5	Cael sat up straight. He had sat up straight in that coach five times now, with his back to the horses and his good coat buttoned, and it had become a thing his spine did by itself when the wheels came off the last switchback onto the cobbles. Karis sat opposite with the document wallet on her knees and a board across the wallet. Beside her Bracken held the house's seal in its box on his lap, with both hands, as another man might have held a hat.
